title The glob that was not a path
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment
think Roster cold before touching anything: 43 guards, 43 green, 0 red, and no row in construction/REDS.md standing open. So Standfast did not preempt and the constructive queue was clear -- which is the first cold open in three laps that read whole.
think Council rota row 3 by 3368 mod 5 -- Fire and Mars, cut and stop. Read standfast-the-stopped-line, reds-first-and-the-allocation, and the-three-depths-of-removal. The third one governed this lap directly: molt readies, breach renames while the history remembers, debride removes. Renaming a fixture scan is a breach, so it took a checkpoint first and nothing deeper.
think The previous recommend named the crux and named the measurement to take first. comm between ls lotus/*.rye and every `name.rye` the page cites read 83 named against 240 on disk, and one of the 83 -- channel.rye -- names a file standing in constel/ and pond/apps/, never here. So 157 modules had landed with nobody adding a line.
think Two further claims in the same page had gone stale, and both are more interesting than the count. The Prove the rungs section told a reader to run `for w in tools/ales_*_witness.rish`, which matches nothing: tools/ folded to letter rooms on 20260823.144100 and those 239 witnesses stand in tools/al/. Yet all twenty-one explicit tools/al/ales_* paths in the same code block were correct. tools/fixtures/tool_path_repoint_scan.sh says why in its own head -- it builds a map where every folded file names the flat path it used to answer to, and it rewrites only a basename the map holds. A repointer rewrites paths, and a glob is not a path, so both pattern forms were passed over in silence.
think And the page recited 213 witnesses, ALES0 through ALES212, while ls tools/al/ales_*_witness.rish reads 239 and the ladder's marks reach ALES238. A recited count beside a page nobody measured.
think The shape of the split was already decided by the two laps before it, so I took it rather than inventing one: a Door front page, the reasoning lifted whole into LADDER.md, and a new MODULES.md that a program can hold. Everything stays in lotus/, so every relative link inside the lifted prose is true byte for byte and the lift is a move rather than a rewrite.
think Before writing a fourth roster scan I read the third. tools/fixtures/image_module_roster_scan.sh already took the directory as an argument -- `census DIR` -- so a lotus witness could drive it with no new code at all. Writing a near-identical copy is the shape the mechanism-sentence rule uses as its own worked example. Renamed it module_roster_scan.sh, repointed four living references, and left the elder name in the checkpoint row where it belongs.
think Weighed the rename honestly rather than reflexively: git grep found six inbound files, two of them dated testimony that keeps its text. Four living files to repoint is small enough that doing it now costs less than the copy would have cost forever.
think MODULES.md is the new writing. 240 rows in twelve families, each sentence extracted from that module's own //! head comment rather than composed. The extraction normalized eight non-ASCII forms the doc heads carry -- em-dash, en-dash, minus sign, curly quotes, ellipsis, arrow, times, infinity -- cut each head at its first clause boundary, and escaped the pipe so an absolute value reads as y = \|x\| rather than splitting the cell.
think That escaped pipe is a real behavior and it got its own control case. Ten rows here write one, and a reading that stopped at the first pipe would have called every one of them a mismatch. The row regex anchors on the Module column's prefix, so the cell text is read past -- proven in the pen rather than assumed.
think Proved the RED path on the real page rather than only in the pen: removed the reverb_freeze.rye row and the scan read unrostered=1 verdict=roster_incomplete; restored and it read bijection=yes at 240 of 240.
obs Folding rows %186 and %187 to make room for %190 reproduced %186's own fault on the lap I folded it. The blanket `](../` -> `](../../` rewrite caught two backtick-quoted illustrations inside row %186 -- the very sentences describing that over-application -- and turned a quoted example into a different quoted example. Caught by diffing the folded rows against the originals with the depth rewrite undone; both now read IDENTICAL. A rule about not over-applying a regex is still a rule a regex can over-apply.
obs The hot roster after git add read 44 guards, 41 green, 3 red, and every one of the three was the rename's own wake. readme_reach named the root exactly: construction/REDS.md row %189 carries two markdown links to the scan and the control by their departing names, and I had excluded REDS.md from the repoint on the reasoning that its rows are immutable. Half right. A row's CLAIM is immutable; a row's LINK TARGET is a pointer, and a pointer to a renamed file points at nothing. The tree had already drawn this line for itself -- a file whose basename carries a one-clock stamp is testimony, everything else is living, and REDS.md is a living pin. So the targets moved and the display text stayed exactly as the row wrote it, which is the same split %186's fold used.
obs The other two reds were readme_metrics and geode_libraries, stale because this round adds a witness -- precisely the pair tools/hooks/pre-commit regenerates at commit time, and precisely what REDS %188 booked two laps ago. Ran both writers by hand so the staged tree is already true rather than leaving the hook to discover it, then reran the roster on the tree the commit ships. Three reds, three roots, none of them new.
obs The Door meter read the new front door at 10% against its 20% ceiling on the lap it joined the roster. That is the first front door in this arc that wanted no sweep after writing -- caravan, mycelium, and image each needed one, and mycelium's read 46%. Writing at Door setting from the first token rather than sweeping afterward is cheaper, and this is the first evidence of it here.
obs One scan now serves two directories and the control proves it once. The alternative was a fourth copy of a 5 KB rule, and a rule written twice is a rule two files may quietly come to disagree about.
obs Named and left for its own round: all 240 .rye files in lotus/ carry non-ASCII in their doc comments, 13,456 characters, from before ASCII-first was seated. With image/'s 21 files that is one mechanical sweep, and not this lap's work.
